ina/charleston-county"],["ARC or PLC in Charleston County","/arc-plc/south-carolina/charleston-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record for Charleston County runs 75 years, 1951 to 2025, on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 11 grids. October to November came in under 90% of normal in 41 of those years, more than any other pair. In 2025 the middle saw 43% of normal in November to December and 123% in July to August. So far in 2026, March to April came in at 14% of normal on the middle, and grid 15500 shows a preliminary estimate of 73.6 for July to August 2026.</p>"}
